            <div xml:id="d372">

                <pb facs="0530" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg428"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2126/56.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the British Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-01-23"><hi rendition="#italic">January 23,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 223.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to inform you, with
                    further reference to your note No. 16 of the 20th instant in connection with the
                    revolutionary outbreak on the island of Haiti, that the Secretary of the Navy
                    informs the department, in response to its request of the 21st instant, that the
                    commanding officer of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Eagle</hi> has been
                    directed by cable to afford protection to British subjects and property pending
                    the arrival at the island of H. M. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Indefatigable</hi>.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
